<misterromdescription>
    <name>Space Ace</name>
    <region>US</region>
    <homebrew>no</homebrew>
    <bootleg>no</bootleg>
    <version>Rev A3</version>
    <alternative></alternative>
    <platform></platform>
    <series>Space Ace</series>
    <year>1983</year>
    <manufacturer>Cinematronics</manufacturer>
    <category>LaserDisc</category>

    <setname>spaceace</setname>
    <parent>spaceace</parent>
    <mameversion>0270</mameversion>
    <rbf>DragonsLair</rbf>
    <about></about>

    <resolution>15kHz</resolution>
    <rotation>horizontal</rotation>
    <flip>no</flip>

    <players>1</players>
    <joystick>4-way</joystick>
    <special_controls></special_controls>
    <num_buttons>1</num_buttons>
    <buttons names="Fire/Energize,Cadet,Captain,Space Ace,Coin,Start 1P,Start 2P,Pause" default="A,B,X,Y,Select,Start,R,L"/>

    <!-- Space Ace DIPs from the Operation & Maintenance Manual, Appendix C. Two 8-bit banks via the AY-3-8910:
           A-points A0-A7 = AY port A = DSW1 = MRA bits 0-7
           B-points B0-B7 = AY port B = DSW2 = MRA bits 8-15
         SA-BOOT-FIX-2026-07-25: default was "00,01" (bit 8 = 1) and the game NEVER talked to the LD.
         ROM proof (spaceace.dasm $0178): ld hl,$A011 / bit 0,(hl) / jp nz,$01F9 -- bit 0 SET means
         SKIP the whole LD routine. $A011 is AY reg $0F = port B = dsw[15:8] (DragonsLair_CPU.sv:258),
         so bit 8 must be 0 to run the LD. Cross-checked against Dragon's Lair, which boots with
         default "20,79": its gate is `bit 3 / jp z` and 0x79 has bit 3 SET -- same port, proven path.
         So the ids below were INVERTED: value 0 is the LD-V1000. Diagnostics = B7 on (bit 15). -->
         SA-BOOT-FIX-2026-07-25. DEFAULTS ARE FROM DAPHNE (authority for this lineage), NOT MAME:
         daphne/game/lair.cpp:290-297  ace::ace()  m_switchA = 0x3D; m_switchB = 0xFE;
         These are the GAME-VISIBLE bytes -- m_switchA/B go straight to $C000 (lair.cpp:634/638) --
         and the core passes dsw to the AY ports raw, so they drop in as the MRA default unchanged.
         SWITCHES ARE ACTIVE LOW (lair.h:65 "enabled low"): a CLEAR bit = that switch ON.
           bit 8  (switchB b0) = 0 -> LD-V1000 selected. MUST be 0 or the game SKIPS the whole LD
                  routine -- ROM proof, spaceace.dasm $0178: ld hl,$A011 / bit 0,(hl) / jp nz,$01F9.
           bit 15 (switchB b7) = 1 -> diagnostics OFF. Setting it 0 runs the CPU test suite
                  (lair.cpp:1072 toggles m_switchB ^= 0x80 to start/stop diagnostics on Ace).
         ⚠️ MAME DISAGREES AND IS WRONG HERE: dlair.cpp defaults DSW2=0x01 (selects LD-PR7820) and
         its PORT_SERVICE(0x80, IP_ACTIVE_HIGH) inverts the diagnostics sense. Prior defaults
         "00,01" (never drove the LD) and "10,00" (booted into diagnostics) both came from MAME.
         ⚠️ The per-bit <dip> ids below were transcribed from MAME and their ON/OFF ORDER is therefore
         UNVERIFIED under active-low -- treat the labels as cosmetic until each is tested. The two
         bytes above are the load-bearing part. -->
    <switches default="3D,FE">
        <!-- DSW1 / bank A (bits 0-7) -->
        <dip bits="0" name="Coinage" ids="2 Coins/1 Credit,3 Coins/1 Credit"/>
        <dip bits="1" name="Lives per Credit" ids="3,5"/>
        <dip bits="2" name="Difficulty (episodes to ramp)" ids="5 - normal,3 - hard"/>
        <dip bits="3" name="Difficulty Increase Rate" ids="Slow,Fast - hard"/>
        <!-- SA-BOOT-FIX-2026-07-25: both were wrong vs MAME. bit4 ids were INVERTED (MAME 0x10:
             0x00=No, 0x10=Yes); bit5 is "Sound Every 8 Attracts" Off/On, not a frequency select. -->
        <dip bits="4" name="Demo Sounds" ids="No,Yes"/>
        <dip bits="5" name="Sound Every 8 Attracts" ids="Off,On"/>
        <!-- A6, A7 not used -->
        <!-- DSW2 / bank B (bits 8-15) -->
        <!-- SA-BOOT-FIX-2026-07-25: ids swapped -- value 0 (not 1) is the LD-V1000; see header note. -->
        <dip bits="8"  name="LaserDisc Player" ids="Pioneer LD-V1000,Pioneer 7820"/>
        <!-- B1, B2, B3 not used -->
        <dip bits="12" name="Free Play (2 credits)" ids="Off,On"/>
        <dip bits="13" name="Unlimited Lives" ids="Off,On"/>
        <dip bits="14" name="Frame Display" ids="Off,On"/>
        <dip bits="15" name="Diagnostics Mode" ids="Off,On"/>
    </switches>

    <!-- Index 0: Main Z80 program ROMs. Rev A3 = 5x 8KB @ 0x0000-0x9FFF (fills the full 0xA000 region). -->
    <rom index="0" md5="none" zip="spaceace.zip|spaceace.zip">
        <part crc="427522d0" name="sa_a3_u1.bin"/>
        <part crc="18d0262d" name="sa_a3_u2.bin"/>
        <part crc="4646832d" name="sa_a3_u3.bin"/>
        <part crc="57db2a79" name="sa_a3_u4.bin"/>
        <part crc="85cbcdc4" name="sa_a3_u5.bin"/>
    </rom>

    <remark>Space Ace (Cinematronics), Dragon's Lair boardset. Index 0 = Z80 game logic only; LaserDisc video handled inside the core (WIP). DIPs need transcription from MAME.</remark>
    <mratimestamp>20260703000000</mratimestamp>
</misterromdescription>
